  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Mosk pointed a shaky paw toward the door, but Lina reached into her pocket, pulling out the last, crisp apple of the season. She set it gently on the step between them, offering it as a peace offering for her intrusion. Mosk stared at the bright fruit for a long time, his eyes softening. Slowly, he stood up, straightened his patched green vest, and stepped onto the first stair, motioning for her to follow."
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "At the base of the stairs, the humming grew into a soft, sorrowful melody. A firefly, large as a robin, lay motionless upon a bed of moss, her golden glow flickering like a dying candle. Mosk’s whiskers trembled as he looked down at her. He whispered that she had been his dearest friend once, but he had failed to bring her medicine during a long winter, and he had guarded this hollow tree ever since, heavy with his own regret."
    }
